<title>UK: UK Treasury says sales show consumer confidence.</title>
<headline>UK Treasury says sales show consumer confidence.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rising UK retail sales show increased confidence among consumers, the British Treasury said.</p>
<p>&quot;Rising high street sales show that people have the cash to spend and the confidence to do it,&quot; Economic Secretary to the Treasury Angela Knight said.</p>
<p>Retail sales rose 0.4 percent month on month in October and 4.1 percent year on year.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
